//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="240")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: diag.sev.warn, mem.region.create.1, mem.region.create.3
//!
//! Issue #192, half one — the counter-example to the never-allocates
//! warning (the code is deliberately not spelled: this file is a
//! fixture for no diagnostic, and the catalog reads these headers).
//! This region block
//! holds no allocation SITE of its own: the only `List` built during
//! its extent is built inside `fill`, and what comes back is an int.
//! The warning fired here anyway ("the region `pass` never allocates …
//! delete the region") because the fact it reads is the in-frame site
//! list, and a callee's allocations are not in it.
//!
//! They are still the region's: `[mem.region.create.3]` (D12) charges
//! a callee's ambient allocations to ITS caller's ambient, which is
//! `pass` while the block is open. Deleting the region on the
//! warning's advice was measured at +82 MB max RSS on the reporter's
//! program. So the analysis gained the second half — no site AND no
//! call in the extent — and this file carries no `warns:` directive,
//! which is the corpus's way of saying every warning here is a bug.
//!
//! `lints/region_never_allocates.lu` is the twin that must still warn:
//! its block calls nothing, so deleting it really is free.

fn fill(n: int) -> int {
    var xs = List[int]()
    var j = 0
    while j < n {
        (mut xs).push(j)
        j = j + 1
    }
    xs.len
}

fn main() -> !int {
    var total = 0
    var i = 0
    while i < 8 {
        region pass { total = total + fill(30) }
        i = i + 1
    }
    print("{total}")
    0
}
